[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: pc15
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: PC15’s host networking configuration (default gateway). Mechanism: For any destination outside its local /24 (e.g., 172.18.50.14 on VLAN 50), PC15 forwards to its configured default gateway. PC15 is set to use 172.18.51.250, which does not exist on VLAN 51, so ARP for the next hop fails and the kernel returns “Destination Host Unreachable” locally.

Localization: On PC15 (eth0), the routing table shows “default via 172.18.51.250 dev eth0.” The ARP table shows “172.18.51.250 dev eth0 FAILED,” confirming the gateway cannot be resolved. Meanwhile, PC15 can reach peers on its own subnet (e.g., PC16) as verified by successful pings, and it can reach 172.18.51.254 directly (the actual SVI/router for VLAN 51), proving L2/L3 upstream is fine. PC16’s routing table correctly points default via 172.18.51.254 and it can reach Laptop4, confirming the network path is healthy.

Root cause: PC15’s default gateway is misconfigured to 172.18.51.250 instead of the correct 172.18.51.254.

Corrective fix: Update PC15’s default route to use 172.18.51.254 and remove the incorrect 172.18.51.250 entry. For example: “ip route del default; ip route add default via 172.18.51.254 dev eth0” (and persist this in the host’s network config). After correction, PC15 will ARP for 172.18.51.254 successfully and route to VLAN 50 normally. === END ===